WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.939
(piano music)

00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:03.379
- In the Dominican Republic,

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:05.848
having kinky or coarse hair

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:10.015
is perceived as something
that's unclean, unkempt.

00:00:11.699 --> 00:00:14.949
Something that is simply not beautiful.

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:18.989
The salon really cares about

00:00:18.989 --> 00:00:21.779
the way that curly hair
is perceived in society.

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.696
And we want to be a part
of that change, fully.

00:00:32.248 --> 00:00:34.008
In 2014, we were trying

00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:36.008
to go into this bar, and

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:39.259
the bouncer said, to my face,

00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:42.048
you can't come in, because of your hair.

00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:43.920
This hair has done nothing to no one.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.328
This hair is part of who I am.

00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:48.995
Why should I put this hair away?

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:51.808
I run as Miss Rizos,

00:00:51.808 --> 00:00:54.031
which means Miss Curls in English.

00:00:54.031 --> 00:00:56.730
And I am the owner of Miss Rizos Salon

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.540
in the Dominican Republic.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.123
So what's goin' on?

00:01:01.051 --> 00:01:03.172
We offer all different types of services

00:01:03.172 --> 00:01:07.339
specifically for naturally
curly Afro-textured hair.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.271
In 2010, I remember

00:01:10.271 --> 00:01:13.820
just straightening the
heck out of my hair.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.540
As my curly hair would grow in,

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.743
I would touch my hair,
feel the curl patterns

00:01:18.743 --> 00:01:20.910
and say, like, what if all of my

00:01:21.871 --> 00:01:23.954
hair would feel this way?

00:01:24.863 --> 00:01:26.612
And that's when I decided that

00:01:26.612 --> 00:01:28.663
it was time to look in the mirror

00:01:28.663 --> 00:01:30.746
and to love myself fully.

00:01:35.906 --> 00:01:38.078
Some of the things I would hear back then

00:01:38.078 --> 00:01:41.328
is, "Did you forget your comb at home?"

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.311
"Did you put your fingers on a socket?"

00:01:46.311 --> 00:01:49.644
I mean, all sorts of really mean things.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.231
But I had all these women just stop me

00:01:53.231 --> 00:01:55.431
and ask me how to curl it,

00:01:55.431 --> 00:01:58.098
how'd I do it, where'd I cut it.

00:01:58.957 --> 00:02:02.365
There was this huge thirst, hunger,

00:02:02.365 --> 00:02:05.082
for a space where women
would be validated.

00:02:05.082 --> 00:02:08.999
And then that led to the
space that I'm in now.

00:02:11.082 --> 00:02:15.249
It's been the most amazing
activism I've done all my life.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.437
To think that with a
brush, a pick, or a comb

00:02:19.437 --> 00:02:22.071
I can empower someone.

00:02:22.071 --> 00:02:24.488
(soft music)

00:02:25.503 --> 00:02:28.420
(electronic music)

